The corpus data in this directory is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0).

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt it for any purpose, including commercially, provided
you give appropriate credit ("Drifterr drift-detection corpus,
https://drifterr.app") and indicate if changes were made.

Why this is open: drift detection is only as honest as the corpus it is measured
on, and a corpus nobody may reuse cannot be checked by anyone. Keeping the
engine proprietary while the evaluation data is open means the accuracy claims
are independently verifiable, and a contributor's annotation work is not locked
into one vendor.

This notice covers the data files only. The Drifterr source code, including the
annotation and evaluation tooling under ../crates/, is licensed separately —
see ../LICENSE.
